# Known scanner/bot-probe paths that don't exist on this site — real 404
# instead of falling through to the SPA catch-all below. Those unknown
# paths used to return 200 with the homepage, which Google Search Console
# flags as a "soft 404". Deliberately a narrow blocklist of well-known
# junk patterns (WordPress admin probes, secret/config file probes), not
# an exhaustive whitelist of every real route — a whitelist risks 404-ing
# a real page if the list is wrong; this only ever removes paths that were
# never real to begin with. See project/plan.md for the reasoning.
/wp-admin/*         /index.html   404
/wp-login.php       /index.html   404
/wp-content/*       /index.html   404
/wp-includes/*      /index.html   404
/wp-json/*          /index.html   404
/xmlrpc.php         /index.html   404
/wp-config.php      /index.html   404
/.env               /index.html   404
/.git/*             /index.html   404
/config.php         /index.html   404
/administrator/*    /index.html   404
/phpmyadmin/*       /index.html   404

